Z||000002||Hank is Here||01-15-2001||12:58 PM||||Good to hear someone has done this.  I may put classic tags on my GT in aother year or two.  Is there any milage restrictions with classic tage.  I know with antique tags I am only allowed to use other cares  about 3000 a year or so.<BR>I don't think that 88GT will can have classic tags yet, Isn't the rule 15 year old?  so wait till 2003||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||01-15-2001||03:20 PM||||That's great news! I tried to get classic tags for one of my '86 Fieros a few years back, but it didn't meet the requirements at that time. I think it needed to be out of production and at least 15 years old or something like that. If that's the case, an '88 still could not get classic tags. As soon as I find a Fiero that's a "keeper" I'll have to look into it.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||Mark||01-15-2001||07:17 PM||||That's outstanding, Todd.  I've considered it for my '86 GT which only sees about 3K miles/yr (39K to date).  Are you completely exempt from emission test fees?  I ask this because the last time I got mine inspected, I requested a exemption due to the low mileage, but this only saved me about $4 on my total bill! I shoulda just has it tested... Also, what insurance company?  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||ToddAsh||01-15-2001||10:14 PM||||Hello, I've got State Farm Insurance.They are great with antiques,Classics and Vettes.I only pay $140.for my '56 chevy and $350. for my '56 Vette.That's for collision,comp and agreed replacement value of $11,000 and $50,000.You know what,my Fiero is a much better toy than eithier of those.I intend to drive it the most,so it has State inspection on it.The other two don't because I don't want some mechanic touching them.I'm thinking of changing the Fiero exhaust system and getting rid of the Cat.I just tagged the car for the first time in 15 years. It's brand new,factory fresh except for new tie,plugs,fuel filter and oil.||||reg||1
Z||000006||ToddAsh||01-15-2001||10:19 PM||||The 79 year old I purchased the car from,bought it and put it in the garage.I drove it Oct and Nov. Now has 15,162 miles on it.Took it down to Cape May yesterday with new 16" tires and wheels from a new Z-34. Most fun car Iv'e ever owned.Thanks for all this great info from everyone. It's nice to know I'm not the only nut out there. Todd||||reg||1
